{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1095429-time-realm","id":1095429,"title":"Time Realm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-22T04:01:43-07:00","id":1095429,"title":"Time Realm","content":"OK, say I want to use Dragon's Ire to use Confound Coils (DI 2) and I want to &quot;hang&quot; it until I say &quot;Shazbot&quot;. Pretty straight forward Art + Realm Diff: 9 (for the modifier realm).<br /> <br /> Now, what if I also want my Confounding Coils to last three times the usual length. Am I using the modifier realm twice... thereby raising the diff to 10... or what? A little help please.<br /> <br /> Oscar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T05:49:36-07:00","id":1095453,"title":"","content":"Good question. I'd rule that it's an additional +1 to the difficulty because you are using the Realm twice, but it could do with clarifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T12:50:04-07:00","id":1095594,"title":"","content":"The table on page 194 indicates that it's a single +1 although I did state it as ambiguous in the errata thread for this reason.<br /> <br /> That said if you don't have Time then the glamour cost is unambiguous. +1 glamour for each realm or level of a realm that you use and don't have. So without Time that's +2 glamour and with Time 1-2 it's +1 glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T13:29:11-07:00","id":1095606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1095429-time-realm?p=1095594#post1095594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The table on page 194 indicates that it's a single +1 although I did state it as ambiguous in the errata thread for this reason.<br /> <br /> That said if you don't have Time then the glamour cost is unambiguous. +1 glamour for each realm or level of a realm that you use and don't have. So without Time that's +2 glamour and with Time 1-2 it's +1 glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not per level. If you have say only Fae 1 (or no Fae at all) it's just one Glamour to target a freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T13:37:15-07:00","id":1095609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1095429-time-realm?p=1095606#post1095606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it's not per level. If you have say only Fae 1 (or no Fae at all) it's just one Glamour to target a freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I wasn't clear. It's only one glamour to target a freehold because the only level of Fae you're using is 5. If, on the other hand, you're casting a single cantrip on a freehold and it's troll knight owner, that's Fae 5 and Fae 2, both of which you don't have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}